  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PATH: Proyecto de Asistencia Tecnica para Trabajadoras del Hogar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A project to address child labor, forced labor, and other labor violations in the domestic work sector in Mexico. The project aims to implement a comprehensive strategy focused on raising awareness about Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work within the domestic work sector in Mexico City and Queretaro. The strategy involves identifying knowledge gaps related to the exploitation of adult and child domestic workers, emphasizing their labor rights, and underscoring the responsibilities of employers as stipulated in Mexico&apos;s recent labor and social security laws, which mandate Social Security coverage for domestic workers since November 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
